{
  "utterance": "Answering the three of you: yes, consent work comes before Jonas's build hours. Nothing gets built until at least some contributors have approved excerpts. I can't confirm prices yet; all I can offer is a labeled estimate request. I'd split the plan: Phase 1 is consent outreach and contributor-chosen excerpts, with a named objections contact, which Mara and Leila should say whether they will take on. Phase 2 is either Jonas's retrieval kiosk or Leila's listening event, depending on how many contributors say yes. Contributor payment and withdrawal turnaround are undecided. Unpaid labor isn't free, so Mara, who would handle objections, and how many hours a week?",
  "cites": ["T1"],
  "memory": "Theo: consent work precedes build; proposes Phase 1 consent/excerpt choice, Phase 2 kiosk or listening event by contributor uptake. Open: contributor payment, objections contact, withdrawal speed, hour estimates from Mara, Jonas, Leila. No budget figures confirmed."
}
